# X0 (PRE-WINDOW, no card reset): the status block, then a PCI bus rescan (a board that dropped off the bus without a by-id link is recovered here, before the stop rule is judged), and nothing deleted. THE RIG PRECONDITION (a STOP job): after the rescan all FOUR boards must be resolved ('=== after the rescan' board list), no card holder, and 'serving containers: none'.
# Anything else stops the window here, before L1's reset refuses on a missing board and the window loses B0's hour. Confirm first that no other window driver is alive (a ship window's driver ends in
# agentstart and must be dead or finished). The status cannot see the node agent's user unit from the runner, so 'serving containers: none' is the evidence that production is down.
# READ: the status block (it runs BEFORE the rescan, so it may show a board the rescan then recovers: judge the board count on the rescan step's after-the-rescan list) and the disk figures. Duration (estimate): 10 min. Stop: a failed status or an unmet precondition stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lookup four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lookup and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lookup commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1
